<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Jehu</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">reigned c. 841–814 BCE</span> · <a href="/centuries/9th-century-bce">9th century BCE</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Jehu was king of Israel from about 841 to 814 BCE. An army commander, he seized the throne in a bloody coup supported by the prophet <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/elisha">Elisha</a>, killing King <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jehoram-of-israel">Joram of Israel</a>, King <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ahaziah-of-judah">Ahaziah of Judah</a> and Queen <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jezebel">Jezebel</a> and wiping out the house of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/omri">Omri</a>. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/black-obelisk-of-shalmaneser-iii">Black Obelisk of Shalmaneser III</a> shows him, or his envoy, bowing before the Assyrian king.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/jehu.jpg" alt="Jehu" width="320" height="272" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Steven G. Johnson · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Jehu_on_the_Black_Obelisk_of_Shalmaneser_III.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
